From: lights-out-fixtures <fixtures@lights-out.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [M42] fixture base: a module with one bandit finding (B307)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The base of the sast-inherited and sast-added-on-red-base fixtures: an unused module calling eval() on its argument, so the base is red at sast before the change under test (docs/adr/0072 §1). No # nosec: the finding must be there.
---
 app/backend/meetups/legacy.py | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 app/backend/meetups/legacy.py

diff --git a/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py b/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5c43b56
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+"""Unused: a module the base already carries, with one bandit finding (B307).
+
+It exists only for two fixtures of `make demo-gates`, sast-inherited and
+sast-added-on-red-base (docs/adr/0072 §1): a base that is red at sast
+before the change under test.
+"""
+
+
+def evaluate(expression: str) -> object:
+    return eval(expression)
